The unchanged compiler uses Lean 4.33.1, commit `819816b2e0a3bf405af45ae5c7af2491d8f5bee6`, with the pinned Mathlib commit `0df444a360eaa60ab8c11dca51a86af692955474`. All compiler invocations retain `-j1`, trust level `-t0`, and `-Ddebug.skipKernelTC=false`.

Ordinary components retain 4,096 MiB / 180 seconds. The existing exact-source `ThetaCertificate5` exception retains 6,144 MiB / 600 seconds; the aggregate and audit retain 6,144 MiB / 300 seconds. The supervisor retained its 12-GiB path-counted allocation limit, 8-GiB free-space floor and 512-MiB per-file bound. It reports no guard event, a measured peak allocation of 2,749,960,192 bytes and minimum observed free storage of 22,019,919,872 bytes.

The earlier interrupted run remains recorded as an executor interruption with a stale historical RUNNING pointer and no delivered controlled-stop signal. The reviewed transport adapter compresses only receipt-bound completed traces and preserves byte-exact recovery. The prior independent review, SHA-256 `9a720c4ca053af8117bc2d9c3defa71b9c70e534a0c7300ffe3452c054431ec5`, covers its missing/corrupt archive, changed/detached receipt, interrupted-state and fail-closed supervisor controls. The adapter and core hashes are unchanged; those negative controls were not rerun as compiler tests during this final review.

